p(17,8,"No doubt we were very foolish, but danger seemed to be all round",
 "The horses are afraid and will not move. Smoke and a red light show the fire is near, and the old hostler comes to help.",
 "The horses were very foolish, Black Beauty says, but danger seemed to be all around. There was nobody they knew and could trust, and everything was strange and not clear. The fresh air that came in through the open door made it easier to breathe. But the rushing sound over their heads grew louder. As he looked up through the bars of his empty rack, he saw a red light moving up and down on the wall. Then he heard a cry of “Fire!” outside, and the old hostler came in quietly and quickly. He got one horse out and went to another. But the flames were playing round the trapdoor, and the roaring overhead was terrible.",
 ["flickering","flames","trapdoor","roaring","dreadful"])
s(17,"had she not heard me outside she would never have had courage",
 "Because if she had not heard me outside, she would never have been brave enough to come out.",
 "'had she not heard' is the same as 'if she had not heard'; 'if' is left out and the helping verb 'had' is put first.")
